Let the CSV stylesheets take a unit per quantity.

xml2detailscsv.xslt and xml2summarycsv.xslt read one parameter, `units`, and
write every column metric (0) or imperial (1). The app lets the diver choose
depth, pressure, volume, temperature and weight on their own, as desktop's
preferences do, and the export has to match what the screens show.

Adds `unitsDepth`, `unitsPressure`, `unitsVolume`, `unitsTemperature` and
`unitsWeight`, each defaulting to `$units`, and tests the matching one where a
value or a column header is converted. A caller that passes only `units` gets
byte for byte what it got before (checked with xsltproc on
dives/abitofeverything.ssrf, both stylesheets, units 0 and 1).

Applied by scripts/vendor-core.mjs to the copies in resources/xslt, with
`patch -p1` inside that directory. The submodule is not touched.

